{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/317451-the-lord-behind-all-mirrors-a-seed","id":317451,"title":"The Lord Behind All Mirrors: a seed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-20T09:39:28-08:00","id":317451,"title":"The Lord Behind All Mirrors: a seed","content":"I'm thinking of playing a Mirrorskin in an online game, and scrawled a few notes about a possible Keeper. Feel free to use, add to, or condemn as you see fit:<br /> <br /> Parts of Arcadia are like the mundane world seen through a glass, darkly. In the Duchy of Lost Reflections, this is literally true. Its ruler, the Lord Behind All Mirrors, looks out at us and hungers for a perfection he can never attain. When he reaches through the silvered glass to grasp at it, his essential nature (all mirrors are flawed) warps and distorts all that he touches. His realm, which can look like anything that has ever been reflected in a mirror, is darkened, warped, and (of course) in reverse.<br /> <br /> Imagine that you are in a cafe. One wall is covered in mirrors, creating an illusion of spaciousness. As you sip your coffee, you spot the reflection of a young woman sitting at a table across the room. She is watching the other diners longingly, and seems on the verge of tears. When you turn to look directly at her, no one is there. You may have just encountered one of the Lord's thralls.<br /> <br /> Many of his subjects are Mirrorskins, who do the bulk of his incomprehensible work, though Fairest Muses are also common. Those few who escape both covet and dread mirrors. They comfort themselves with the knowledge that their old master can gaze through but one at a time.<br /> <br /> Notes: The Lord (he can appear as a Lady, but his gaze always feels disconcertingly male) has no fixed appearance, but can look like any living being who is currently being reflected in a mirror. If you've ever looked in a mirror and felt somehow disconnected or <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Depersonalization_disorder\" target=\"_blank\">depersonalized</a>, He may be your reflection. When the feeling passes, His attention has moved elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3629-bibliomancer","user":"Bibliomancer","date":".  Corrected minor typos 11-20-2014, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3629-bibliomancer","name":"Bibliomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}